{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The skill references are relative. Let me look at the execution-controls.md reference to understand workflowScript format precisely. Actually, I already have a good understanding from the subagent tool description. The workflowScript is a JavaScript statement body like:\n\n```\nreturn runs.run('main', {agent:'worker', task:'...'})\n```\n\nor sequential:\n\n```\nconst a = await runs.run('task1', {agent:'worker', task:'...'});\nconst b = await runs.run('task2', {agent:'worker', task:'...'});\nreturn {a: a.output, b: b.output};\n```\n\nThe test regex is `runs\\.run\\(\\s*['\\\"](task\\d+)['\\\"]`. So I need `runs.run('task1', {...})` literal.\n\nNow, let me design the exact output. The doing prompt's workflowScript orchestration section should contain something like:\n\n```\n## pi 编排（workflowScript）\n\n你是 parent 编排者。必须调用 `subagent` 工具触发以下 workflowScript（一次触发，内部按依赖拓扑顺序执行，await 强制顺序）：\n\n```javascript\nconst workflowScript = `\nconst task1 = await runs.run('task1', {agent:'worker', task:'...'});\nconst task2 = await runs.run('task2', {agent:'worker', task:'...'});\nreturn {task1: task1.output, task2: task2.output};\n`;\n```\n```\n\nActually, the important thing is the literal `runs.run('task1'` and `runs.run('task2'` appear in topological order (task1 before task2), and `workflowScript` keyword appears.\n\nLet me check the exact regex in the test again:\n- `r'workflowScript'` — literal word\n- `r'runs\\.run'` — literal `runs.run`\n- `extract_orchestrated_task_ids` uses `r\"runs\\.run\\(\\s*['\\\"](task\\d+)['\\\"]\"` — so `runs.run('task1'` or `runs.run(\"task1\"`.\n\nSo the prompt must contain these.\n\nNow, let me design the builder code. I'll add a new function to the builder package (or a new file) that:\n1. Given `doingDir`, `planDir`, reads tasks.json (or generates from plan).\n2. Filters success.\n3. Computes topological order.\n4. Generates the workflowScript string.\n\nThen in `BuildDoing` and `SaveDoingPrompt`, set a new template variable like `{{orchestration_section}}` (or `pi_orchestration`).\n\nWait, but the doing template currently doesn't have an orchestration section. I need to add it to the template. The task KR4 says \"同步改写 `templates/doing.md` 第二步\" to remove check_command/check_step_header and add pi hook gate / workflowScript orchestration semantics.\n\nLet me plan the template change for doing.md:\n\nCurrent doing.md has:\n```\n{{check_step_header}}\n\n`{{rick_bin_path}} tools {{check_command}} {{job_id}}`\n\ncheck pass 后才算完成。\n```\n\nI need to change this to reflect the new gate (pi hook + workflowScript orchestration). And add an orchestration section.\n\nLet me design a clean doing.md template:\n\n```\n# Rick 项目执行阶段\n\n## 角色定义\n\n你是一个资深的软件工程师，同时是本次 job 的 parent 编排者。你的任务是按依赖拓扑顺序调度 subagent 执行各 task，完成编码工作。\n\n---\n\n## 先验知识（执行前必读）\n\n{{loops_context}}\n\n{{skills_context}}\n\n---\n\n## Job 上下文\n\n{{debug_context}}\n\n---\n\n{{task_info_section}}\n\n{{requirement}}\n\n---\n\n## 第一步：执行 Doing Loop\n\n{{doing_loop_content}}\n\n{{import_ctx_content}}\n\n{{orchestration_section}}\n\n{{gate_section}}\n```\n\nActually, I should be careful to keep the doing_loop content (the Default Loop steps). The task's own prompt shows the doing loop content includes \"第一步：执行 Doing Loop\" etc. Let me keep it minimal but ensure the required variables are present.\n\nActually, let me minimize the template changes. The key required changes:\n1. Remove `check_step_header` and `check_command` (they're dead code to remove).\n2. Add orchestration section (workflowScript).\n3. Add gate section (pi hook gate).\n\nLet me look at what variables are currently set in BuildDoing/SaveDoingPrompt:\n- task_info_section\n- requirement\n- grilling_section\n- import_ctx_content\n- session_wrap_section\n- loops_context\n- skills_context\n- doing_loop_content\n- loop_step_header\n- check_step_header\n- debug_context\n- rick_bin_path\n- check_command\n- job_id\n\nI need to:\n- Remove `check_step_header` and `check_command`.\n- Add `orchestration_section` (or `workflow_script`).\n- Possibly keep `rick_bin_path`, `job_id`.\n\nBut wait — the easy prompt (BuildEasy, SaveEasyPrompt) also uses the doing template and sets `check_step_header` and `check_command`. I need to be careful: easy mode also uses the doing template. Let me check what easy mode needs. The task says \"清理 `easy_prompt.go`/`doing_prompt.go` 中 `check_command`/`check_step_header` 的死代码设置\". So I need to remove these from easy too.\n\nActually, easy mode still needs an easy_check gate. But the task KR4 says \"同步改写 `templates/doing.md` 第二步... 删除 `check_step_header`/`check_command`/`{{check_command}}`/`plan_check`/`doing_check`/`easy_check` 的注入与引用，改为 pi hook 门禁 / workflowScript 编排语义\".\n\nHmm, so even easy_check references should be removed from the doing template. But easy mode uses the same template. Let me think about how easy mode works.\n\nActually, looking more carefully: the easy mode uses `doing` template with `check_command: easy_check`. If I remove `check_command` from the template, easy mode also loses its gate reference. But the task says easy_check is in the \"删除引用\" list too.\n\nWait, but `tools_easy_check.go` — actually there's no separate tools_easy_check.go; it's in `tools_doing_check.go` (the `NewEasyCheckCmd` is in tools_doing_check.go). Let me check: the task KR4 says \"删除 `internal/cmd/tools_doing_check.go`、`internal/cmd/tools_plan_check.go`\". And \"`learning_check`/`dream_check` 存活\". And \"`easy_check`\" — hmm, the test only checks for `tools_doing_check.go` and `tools_plan_check.go` deletion.\n\nWait, but `NewEasyCheckCmd` is defined in tools_doing_check.go. If I delete tools_doing_check.go, then easy_check command is gone. But the task says \"`learning_check`/`dream_check` 存活\" and doesn't mention easy_check surviving. And KR4 says \"`easy_check` 的注入与引用\" should be removed.\n\nHmm wait, let me re-read: \"同步改写 `templates/plan.md` 第 8 步、`templates/doing.md` 第二步、`skills/doing_loop.md`（删除 `check_step_header`/`check_command`/`{{check_command}}`/`plan_check`/`doing_check`/`easy_check` 的注入与引用，改为 pi hook 门禁 / workflowScript 编排语义）\".\n\nSo `easy_check` reference should be removed from templates. But is `easy_check` command itself deleted? The task's deletion list is: \"`internal/executor`（...）、`internal/parser`、`internal/git`、`internal/logging`、`internal/cmd/tools_doing_check.go`、`internal/cmd/tools_plan_check.go`\". \n\n`NewEasyCheckCmd` is in `tools_doing_check.go`. If I delete that file, `NewEasyCheckCmd` is undefined, and `tools.go` references it. So I need to remove `NewEasyCheckCmd` registration from tools.go too.\n\nBut wait — does anything else use easy_check? Let me check. The `easy` command flow. Let me search for easy_check references.\n\nActually, let me focus. The task says tools.go should remove `NewPlanCheckCmd`/`NewDoingCheckCmd`/`NewEasyCheckCmd` registrations. KR4: \"同步删除/改写 `tools.go` 中对 `NewPlanCheckCmd`/`NewDoingCheckCmd`/`NewEasyCheckCmd` 的注册（否则 cmd 编译 `undefined`）\".\n\nSo I need to:\n- Delete `tools_doing_check.go` (contains NewDoingCheckCmd AND NewEasyCheckCmd).\n- Delete `tools_plan_check.go` (contains NewPlanCheckCmd).\n- Remove registrations of NewPlanCheckCmd, NewDoingCheckCmd, NewEasyCheckCmd from tools.go.\n- Keep NewLearningCheckCmd, NewDreamCheckCmd (in tools_learning_check.go, tools_dream_check.go).\n\nWait, but where is NewEasyCheckCmd? It's in tools_doing_check.go. And the task lists only tools_doing_check.go and tools_plan_check.go for deletion. So NewEasyCheckCmd goes away with tools_doing_check.go. That's fine.\n\nBut the easy handler (handler/easy.go) — does it reference easy_check? Let me check. Actually the easy prompt sets `check_command: easy_check`. If I remove the check_command variable from the template, easy mode won't have a check. But the task explicitly says to remove easy_check references. So easy mode's gate also becomes \"pi hook gate\" semantics.\n\nOK. Let me now also check: does the doing command (non-easy) still need to work end-to-end? The test only tests dry-run (which generates prompt) and the gate helper.py directly. It doesn't run an actual doing execution with pi. So I mainly need:\n1. DoingDryRun to output workflowScript + runs.run orchestration.\n2. Gate helper.py to work.\n3. go build + go test pass.\n4. runtime.Run returns error when not settled.\n\nLet me now check what `handler.Doing` needs to do for the actual (non-dry-run) path. The test doesn't run `rick doing job_N` (non-dry-run). But `go build` must compile, and handler.Doing must not import executor/git/parser and must have MaxRetries. Also the source-level assertion checks `doing.go` for `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/executor\"`, `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/git\"`, `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"` and `MaxRetries`.\n\nSo I need to rewrite handler.Doing to:\n1. Not import executor/git/parser.\n2. Have `MaxRetries` (e.g., from cfg.MaxRetries).\n3. Orchestrate: builder → runtime.Run → gate helper.py → retry loop.\n\nLet me now think about the new handler.Doing flow in detail:\n\n```go\nfunc Doing(jobID string, opts Options) error {\n    cfg := config.LoadConfig()\n    rickDir := workspace.GetRickDir()\n    jobDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID)\n    planDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"plan\")\n    doingDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"doing\")\n    // validate plan dir\n    // MkdirAll doingDir\n    \n    // ensure tasks.json exists (builder generates initial draft if missing)\n    // build prompt (builder produces workflowScript orchestration + gate instructions)\n    \n    maxRetries := cfg.MaxRetries\n    if maxRetries <= 0 { maxRetries = 3 }  // or 5\n    \n    for attempt := 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++ {\n        // build prompt for remaining pending tasks\n        promptFile, method, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(...)\n        // run pi\n        sessionID, trace, err := runti