untime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...).Run(method, promptFile, cfg)\n        if err != nil { continue }  // retry\n        // gate\n        if gateErr := runGate(doingDir); gateErr != nil {\n            // retry\n            continue\n        }\n        return nil\n    }\n    return error\n}\n```\n\nBut wait — the actual doing run with pi requires pi to do the work, and the gate checks tasks.json. This is a real workflow but I don't need it to actually be fully functional for the test (only dry-run + compile + gate helper). But it should be reasonably correct.\n\nActually, let me think about what \"correct\" means here. The task is a huge refactor. The main correctness criteria are:\n1. `go build ./cmd/rick` succeeds.\n2. `go test` for key packages passes.\n3. Gate helper.py works.\n4. Dry-run outputs orchestration.\n5. handler.Doing source-level: no executor/git/parser import, has MaxRetries.\n6. Templates don't reference act-path.md.\n7. runtime.Run returns error when not settled.\n8. 6 packages deleted.\n\nLet me also consider: the `easy.go` handler and `plan.go` handler might reference parser/executor. Let me check handler/plan.go and handler/easy.go, and handler/ctrl.go.\n\nLet me search for all imports of the packages to delete across the codebase (excluding test files I'll also handle).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_sOsoyZUOy2DOJKcuZAhe0299","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== executor imports ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/executor\" --include='*.go' internal/ cmd/ pkg/ && echo \"=== parser imports ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/parser\" --include='*.go' internal/ cmd/ pkg/ && echo \"=== git imports ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/git\" --include='*.go' internal/ cmd/ pkg/ && echo \"=== logging imports ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/logging\" --include='*.go' internal/ cmd/ pkg/ && echo \"=== agent imports ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/agent\" --include='*.go' intern