{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The easy handler uses `builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveEasyPrompt`. So the `prompt/easy_prompt.go`'s `GenerateEasyPromptFile`/`GenerateEasyPrompt` are dead code (only used by tests). But `prompt` package still needs `loadDebugContextLocal`? No — that's in easy_prompt.go, only used by easy_prompt.go itself.\n\nWait, but `builder/pibuilder.go`'s `BuildEasy`/`SaveEasyPrompt` set `check_step_header` and `check_command`. I need to remove those. Let me check what other dead code is in `easy_prompt.go` that's referenced by builder. Actually, the builder has its own `buildRequirementSection`, `buildGrillingSection`, `buildCtxSection`, `buildSessionWrapSection`, `stripYAMLFrontmatter`, `renderDoingLoop`, `readFileOrDefault`, `debugDirPath`, `taskFilePath`, `resolvePromptsDir` — these are duplicated in builder. So `prompt/easy_prompt.go` and `prompt/doing_prompt.go` are essentially DEAD CODE now (after task5/6 migrated to builder).\n\nWait, but `easy_prompt_test.go` and `debug_skill_verify_test.go` test `GenerateEasyPromptFile`. And `doing_prompt_test.go` etc test `GenerateDoingPrompt`. These are all in the prompt package and import parser.\n\nGiven the task says to decouple prompt from parser (and delete OKR/SPEC dead code + tests), the cleanest approach is:\n\n**Delete the dead `prompt` functions that import parser, and their tests.**\n\nSpecifically, delete/rewrite:\n1. `internal/prompt/doing_prompt.go` — remove `GenerateDoingPrompt`, `GenerateDoingPromptFile`, `formatTaskInfoSection`, `formatDebugContext`, `formatKeyResults`, `readAndAppend`. Keep `loadDoingLoopContent` (used by easy_prompt.go) and `resolvePromptsDir`? Let me check: `resolvePromptsDir` is used by doing_prompt.go's GenerateDoingPromptFile only. And `loadDoingLoopContent` is used by easy_prompt.go. Hmm.\n\nActually wait, let me check if `prompt/doing_prompt.go`'s `loadDoingLoopContent` and `stripYAMLFrontmatter` are used elsewhere. `stripYAMLFrontmatter` is defined in BOTH `easy_prompt.go` and `pibuilder.go`. And `prompt/doing_prompt.go` has `loadDoingLoopContent` which is used by `easy_prompt.go` (line `builder.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", loadDoingLoopContent(domainDir, debugSkillFile))`).\n\nSo `loadDoingLoopContent` IS used by easy_prompt.go (which is itself dead but tested). This is getting circular.\n\nLet me step back and think about the cleanest minimal plan:\n\n**Approach: Keep the prompt package but remove parser dependency entirely.**\n\n1. `context.go`: ContextManager — remove OKR/SPEC fields+methods. Change `Task` and `Debug` fields to not use parser types. Actually, the simplest: remove `Task`, `Debug`, `OKRInfo`, `SPECInfo`, `OKRRaw`, `SPECRaw` fields and ALL their methods (LoadTask, GetTask, IsTaskLoaded, LoadDebugFromContent, LoadDebugFromFile, SetDebugRaw, GetDebugRaw, GetDebug, HasDebugEntries, LoadOKR*, LoadSPEC*, GetOKR*, GetSPEC*, HasOKR*, HasSPEC*). Keep `jobID`, `History`, `LoadHistory`, `LoadHistoryFromFile`, `GetHistory`, `GetJobID`, `NewContextManager`.\n\nWait but ContextManager's `GetDebugRaw`/`SetDebugRaw`/`GetDebug`/`GetJobID` are used by `doing_prompt.go`'s `GenerateDoingPrompt`. If I delete those functions too, then ContextManager becomes minimal. And `GenerateDoingPrompt` becomes dead.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider: maybe the cleanest is to DELETE `doing_prompt.go` entirely (its `GenerateDoingPrompt`/`GenerateDoingPromptFile` are dead) and DELETE the corresponding tests. But `loadDoingLoopContent` in doing_prompt.go is used by easy_prompt.go. So I'd need to move `loadDoingLoopContent` to easy_prompt.go or keep a minimal doing_prompt.go with just the shared helpers.\n\nActually, let me simplify the whole thing. Given the massive scope, I'll take these concrete steps:\n\n### Plan A: Minimize prompt package surface\n\n1. **`doing_prompt.go`**: Delete the entire file content except `loadDoingLoopContent` (move it into a small file or keep). Actually, I'll keep `doing_prompt.go` but rewrite it to only contain `loadDoingLoopContent` (no parser import, no `GenerateDoingPrompt`).\n\nWait — but `stripYAMLFrontmatter` is defined in easy_prompt.go (same package). And `loadDoingLoopContent` uses `stripYAMLFrontmatter`. So keeping `loadDoingLoopContent` in doing_prompt.go works.\n\n2. **`easy_prompt.go`**: \n   - Remove `parser` import. Replace `parser.ExtractBugFrontmatter` in `loadDebugContextLocal` with a local inline implementation.\n   - Remove `check_step_header` and `check_command` setVariable calls (dead). Also `loop_step_header`? The task says remove `check_command`/`check_step_header`. `loop_step_header` is fine (it's in doing.md template).\n   - But wait — if I remove `check_step_header` from the template (doing.md), then the `loop_step_header`/`check_step_header` variables are no longer in the template. So `builder.SetVariable(\"check_step_header\", ...)` becomes a no-op (harmless but the task says remove). Let me remove `check_command` and `check_step_header` SetVariable calls.\n\n3. **`context_helpers.go`**: Remove `formatOKRContent`, `formatSPECContent`, `formatCompletedWork`? Wait, `formatCompletedWork` doesn't use parser. The task says remove `formatOKRContent`/`formatSPECContent` (they use parser.ContextInfo). `formatCompletedWork` takes `[]string` — no parser. But is it used? Let me check. Actually, let me grep for formatCompletedWork usage.\n\nLet me be efficient and check a few usages.\n\nActually, let me just grep for all function usage in the prompt package to determine dead code precisely.\n\nLet me now also read the remaining test files fully to understand what I need to rewrite. But this is a huge amount. Let me take a more surgical approach:\n\nGiven time constraints, I'll:\n1. Rewrite `context.go` to remove parser (keep ContextManager minimal but compatible).\n2. Rewrite `doing_prompt.go` to remove parser and the dead functions.\n3. Rewrite `easy_prompt.go` to remove parser.\n4. Rewrite `context_helpers.go` to remove formatOKRContent/formatSPECContent.\n5. Delete/rewrite the 5 test files that import parser.\n6. Also `context_helpers_test.go` — check if it tests formatOKRContent/formatSPECContent.\n\nLet me read context_helpers_test.go and check formatCompletedWork usage."}}
