ch I'm rewriting).\n\nOK. Let me design the orchestration file and update pibuilder.go.\n\nLet me write `internal/builder/orchestration.go`.\n\nKey functions:\n1. `pendingOrchTasks(doingDir, planDir string) []orchTask` — returns pending tasks with deps.\n2. `topoSort(orchTasks) ([]string, error)` — Kahn's algorithm.\n3. `renderWorkflowScript(taskIDs []string, planDir string) string` — produces the workflowScript section text.\n\nFor reading tasks.json, I'll use workspace.LoadTasksJSON. For plan scan, minimal parsing.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nActually, I realize there might be an import cycle issue if builder imports workspace and workspace imports builder. Let me verify workspace doesn't import builder. workspace imports: encoding/json, fmt, os, path/filepath, sort, strconv, strings, bufio. No builder. Good.\n\nNow, the orchestration section content. I need to include literal `workflowScript` and `runs.run('taskN'`. Let me produce:\n\n```\n## pi 编排（workflowScript）\n\n你是本次 job 的 parent 编排者（单写者）。必须调用 `subagent` 工具，传入下面的 `workflowScript` 触发编排执行。编排按依赖拓扑顺序，`await` 强制顺序（被依赖 task 先执行）；每个 task 完成后立即由对应 worker commit 并回传 commit_hash。\n\n```javascript\nconst workflowScript = `\nconst task1 = await runs.run('task1', {agent:'worker', task:'请按 <task1.md 路径> 执行 task1 并完成后 commit'});\nconst task2 = await runs.run('task2', {agent:'worker', task:'...'});\nreturn {task1: task1.output, task2: task2.output};\n`;\n```\n\ntrigger 编排：把上述 `workflowScript` 作为 `subagent` 工具调用的 `workflowScript` 参数。\n```\n\nWait, the regex `runs\\.run\\(\\s*['\\\"](task\\d+)['\\\"]` needs `runs.run('task1'`. My line `const task1 = await runs.run('task1', {agent:'worker', ...})` contains `runs.run('task1'`. Good.\n\nBut I need to be careful with the template variable escaping. The section is just a string I inject into the doing template via a new variable `{{orchestration_section}}`.\n\nLet me write the render function to produce clean text. The workflowScript is a JS string template. I'll produce the section as a Go string.\n\nLet me write it carefully:\n\n```go\nfunc renderWorkflowSection(pendingIDs []string, planDir string) string {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tsb.WriteString(\"## pi 编排（workflowScript）\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"你是本次 job 的 parent 编排者（单写者）。你必须调用 `subagent` 工具触发以下 `workflowScript`（一次触发，内部按依赖拓扑顺序执行，`await` 强制顺序，被依赖 task 先执行）。\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"```javascript\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"const workflowScript = `\\n\")\n\tfor _, id := range pendingIDs {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf(\"const %s = await runs.run('%s', {agent:'worker', task:'按 %s 执行 %s，完成后 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent 写入 tasks.json'});\\n\", id, id, filepath.Join(planDir, id+\".md\"), id))\n\t}\n\tsb.WriteString(\"return {\")\n\tfor i, id := range pendingIDs {\n\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\", \")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(id + \": \" + id + \".output\")\n\t}\n\tsb.WriteString(\"};\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"`;\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"```\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"把上述 `workflowScript` 作为 `subagent` 工具的 `workflowScript` 参数触发编排执行。\\n\")\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n```\n\nThis produces the needed text. Good.\n\nNow `topoSort` (Kahn):\n```go\nfunc topoSort(tasks []orchTask) ([]string, error) {\n\t// build graph: task ID -> dependents (edges from dependency to dependent)\n\t// in-degree = number of unresolved dependencies within the pending set\n\tpending := map[string]bool{}\n\tdeps := map[string][]string{}\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tpending[t.ID] = true\n\t\tdeps[t.ID] = t.Dependencies\n\t}\n\t// in-degree count = number of dependencies that are in the pending set\n\tinDegree := map[string]int{}\n\t// dependents: for each task, for each dep in pending, dep -> task\n\tdependents := map[string][]string{}\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tfor _, d := range t.Dependencies {\n\t\t\tif pending[d] {\n\t\t\t\tinDegree[t.ID]++\n\t\t\t\tdependents[d] = append(dependents[d], t.ID)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// queue = tasks with inDegree 0, in deterministic order (sort IDs)\n\tqueue := []string{}\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tif inDegree[t.ID] == 0 {\n\t\t\tqueue = append(queue, t.ID)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(queue)\n\tvar result []string\n\tfor len(queue) > 0 {\n\t\tcur := queue[0]\n\t\tqueue = queue[1:]\n\t\tresult = append(result, cur)\n\t\tfor _, dep := range dependents[cur] {\n\t\t\tinDegree[dep]--\n\t\t\tif inDegree[dep] == 0 {\n\t\t\t\tqueue = append(queue, dep)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\t// keep queue sorted for determinism\n\t\tsort.Strings(queue)\n\t}\n\tif len(result) != len(tasks) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cycle detected in pending tasks\")\n\t}\n\treturn result, nil\n}\n```\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety with sorting: if I sort the queue each iteration, deterministic. But the test expects \"task1 before task2\" (task2 depends on task1). With all pending [task1 (no dep), task2 (dep task1), task3 (no dep)], inDegree: task1=0, task2=1, task3=0. queue sorted = [task1, task3]. Process task1 → result=[task1], decrement task2 → inDegree task2=0, queue=[task3, task2] sorted=[task2, task3]. Process task2 → result=[task1,task2]. Then task3 → [task1,task2,task3]. Good, task1 before task2.\n\nBut wait, the test also needs task3 present. Yes.\n\nFor job_2 (task1 success removed, task2 dep task1, task3 no dep): pending = [task2 (dep task1), task3 (no dep)]. inDegree: task2: dep task1 not in pending → 0. task3: 0. queue sorted = [task2, task3]. result = [task2, task3]. Good, no task1.\n\nNow the `pendingOrchTasks` reading. When tasks.json exists, use workspace.LoadTasksJSON and filter status != success. When missing, scan plan dir.\n\nFor scanning plan dir, I need to parse \"# 依赖关系\". Let me write a minimal extractor.\n\nAlso, when tasks.json is missing, the KR1 says the builder should write the initial tasks.json draft. But for dry-run, we shouldn't necessarily write. However, the test for job_1 (no tasks.json) just needs the orchestration to include all 3 tasks. So I don't need to write tasks.json in dry-run. But for the real `Doing` (non-dry-run), the builder should generate tasks.json. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me keep it simple: the orchestration generator reads tasks.json if present, else scans plan. For the real Doing flow, I'll add a separate step in handler.Doing to ensure tasks.json exists (generate initial draft via a builder function). But to keep things minimal and since the test only checks dry-run + gate helper, I can have the builder's orchestration generation ALSO write the initial tasks.json draft when missing (best-effort, ignoring errors). Actually, writing in dry-run is a side effect but harmless in temp dirs. But it's semantically wrong for dry-run.\n\nLet me think about what's cleanest:\n- `BuildDoing` (dry-run path, returns instance string) — should NOT write files. Just read tasks.json or scan plan for orchestration.\n- `SaveDoingPrompt` (real path) — could write tasks.json draft. But actually the handler.Doing will handle tasks.json creation.\n\nFor simplicity and correctness of the test, I'll make the orchestration generation READ-ONLY (no file writes). The handler.Doing will ensure tasks.json exists by calling a builder function `EnsureTasksJSON` (which writes the initial draft). But actually, the test doesn't test the real Doing path, so I can be minimal.\n\nLet me define in builder:\n- `EnsureTasksJSON(doingDir, planDir string) error` — if tasks.json missing, scan plan and write draft.\n- `BuildOrchestrationSection(doingDir, planDir string) string` — read tasks.json (or scan) and produce the workflowScript section.\n\nActually, let me combine: a single function `buildOrchestration(doingDir, planDir string) string` that reads tasks.json or scans plan. And a separate `EnsureTasksJSON` for the handler.\n\nLet me now also think: the handler.Doing needs to generate the initial tasks.json. I'll write it there directly (or via builder). Let me put `EnsureTasksJSON` in builder.\n\nOK let me write the orchestration.go file now.\n\nFor the plan scan dependency parsing, I'll extract the \"# 依赖关系\" section. Let me write a helper `parseDepsFromTaskMD(content string) []string`.\n\nActually, let me also consider: the tasks.json in the real job has `dependencies` field. When tasks.json exists, I use it. When missing, I scan plan. Good.\n\nLet me write it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_8o4rHYaP8oKnbmTbl2NH6213","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/builder/orchestration.go","content":"package builder\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\n)\n\n// orchTask is the minimal task node for the doing orchestration: id + direct\n// dependencies. It is computed at prompt-generation time (rick-side) because the\n// pi workflowScript sandbox has no filesystem access — \"skip completed\" must be\n// resolved before the prompt is assembled.\ntype orchTask struct {\n\tID           string\n\tDependencies []string\n}\n\n// buildOrchestrationSection renders the pi workflowScript orchestration for the\n// pending (non-success) tasks in topological order. When doing/tasks.json does\n// not exist yet, it falls back to scanning plan/task*.md (all pending).\nfunc buildOrchestrationSection(doingDir, planDir string) string {\n\ttasks := pendingOrchTasks(doingDir, planDir)\n\tids, err := topoSortOrch(tasks)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// A cycle in the pending set is a plan error; surface it inline rather\n\t\t// than failing prompt generation so the agent can report it.\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"## pi 编排（workflowScript）\\n\\n无法生成编排：依赖存在环（%v）。请先修正 plan 的依赖关系。\\n\", err)\n\t}\n\tif len(ids) == 0 {\n\t\treturn \"## pi 编排（workflowScript）\\n\\n所有 task 均已完成（status=success），无待执行的编排。\\n\"\n\t}\n\treturn renderWorkflowSection(ids, planDir)\n}\n\n// pendingOrchTasks returns pending tasks (status != success) with dependencies,\n// reading doing/tasks.json first and falling back to plan/task*.md.\nfunc pendingOrchTasks(doingDir, planDir string) []orchTask {\n\tif doingDir != \"\" {\n\t\tif tj, err := workspace.LoadTasksJSON(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"tasks.json\")); err == nil {\n\t\t\tout := make([]orchTask, 0, len(tj.Tasks))\n\t\t\tfor _, t := range tj.Tasks {\n\t\t\t\tif t.Status == \"success\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, orchTask{ID: t.TaskID, Dependencies: t.Dependencies})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn out\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn scanPlanOrchTasks(planDir)\n}\n\n// scanPlanOrchTasks scans plan/task*.md and extracts the # 依赖关系 section for\n// each (all pending — no tasks.json yet).\nfunc scanPlanOrchTasks(planDir string) []orchTask {\n\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(planDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tvar names []string\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tif e.IsDir() || !strings.HasPrefix(e.Name(), \"task\") || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".md\") {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tnames = append(names, e.Name())\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(names)\n\n\tvar out []orchTask\n\tfor _, name := range names {\n\t\tid := strings.TrimSuffix(name, \".md\")\n\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(planDir, name))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tout = append(out, orchTask{ID: id})\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tout = append(out, orchTask{ID: id, Dependencies: parseDepsSection(string(data))})\n\t}\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// parseDepsSection extracts the \"# 依赖关系\" section content and splits it into\n// task ids (comma-separated). \"无\"/\"无依赖\"/\"none\"/\"-\" and empties are dropped.\nfunc parseDepsSection(content string) []string {\n\tsection := extractSection(content, \"# 依赖关系\")\n\tif section == \"\" {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tvar deps []string\n\tfor _, part := range strings.Split(section, \",\") {\n\t\tt := strings.TrimSpace(part)\n\t\tif t == \"\" || isNoDepToken(t) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tdeps = append(deps, t)\n\t}\n\treturn deps\n}\n\n// extractSection returns the content under a markdown heading until the next\n// same-or-higher-level heading (mirrors the deleted parser's minimal behavior).\nfunc extractSection(content, heading string) string {\n\tlines := strings.Split(content, \"\\n\")\n\tvar out []string\n\tfound := false\n\tlevel := 0\n\tfor _, line := range lines {\n\t\ttrimmed := strings.TrimSpace(line)\n\t\tif trimmed == heading {\n\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\tlevel = headingLevel(trimmed)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(trimmed, \"#\") && headingLevel(trimmed) <= level {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tout = append(out, line)\n\t}\n\tfor len(out) > 0 && strings.TrimSpace(out[0]) == \"\" {\n\t\tout = out[1:]\n\t}\n\tfor len(out) > 0 && strings.TrimSpace(out[len(out)-1]) == \"\" {\n\t\tout = out[:len(out)-1]\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Join(out, \"\\n\")\n}\n\nfunc headingLevel(line string) int {\n\treturn len(line) - len(strings.TrimLeft(line, \"#\"))\n}\n\nfunc isNoDepToken(s string) bool {\n\ttrimmed := strings.Trim(s, \"()（）\")\n\tswitch strings.ToLower(trimmed) {\n\tcase \"无\", \"无依赖\", \"none\", \"null\", \"nil\", \"n/a\", \"na\", \"-\":\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// topoSortOrch is an inlined Kahn topological sort over the pending tasks.\nfunc topoSortOrch(tasks []orchTask) ([]string, error) {\n\tif len(tasks) == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil, nil\n\t}\n\tpending := make(map[string]bool, len(tasks))\n\tinDegree := make(map[string]int, len(tasks))\n\tdependents := make(map[string][]string, len(tasks))\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tpending[t.ID] = true\n\t}\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tfor _, d := range t.Dependencies {\n\t\t\tif pending[d] {\n\t\t\t\tinDegree[t.ID]++\n\t\t\t\tdependents[d] = append(dependents[d], t.ID)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar queue []string\n\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\tif inDegree[t.ID] == 0 {\n\t\t\tqueue = append(queue, t.ID)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(queue)\n\n\tvar result []string\n\tfor len(queue) > 0 {\n\t\tcur := queue[0]\n\t\tqueue = queue[1:]\n\t\tresult = append(result, cur)\n\t\tfor _, dep := range dependents[cur] {\n\t\t\tinDegree[dep]--\n\t\t\tif inDegree[dep] == 0 {\n\t\t\t\tqueue = append(queue, dep)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tsort.Strings(queue)\n\t}\n\tif len(result) != len(tasks) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cycle detected\")\n\t}\n\treturn result, nil\n}\n\n// renderWorkflowSection renders the workflowScript + runs.run orchestration for\n// the given topological task order.\nfunc renderWorkflowSection(ids []string, planDir string) string {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tsb.WriteString(\"## pi 编排（workflowScript）\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"你是本次 job 的 parent 编排者（单写者）。必须调用 `subagent` 工具，把下面的 `workflowScript` 作为其 `workflowScript` 参数触发编排执行（一次触发，内部按依赖拓扑顺序执行，`await` 强制顺序，被依赖 task 先执行；每个 task 完成后由 worker 立即 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent 写入 tasks.json）。\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"```javascript\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"const workflowScript = `\\n\")\n\tfor _, id := range ids {\n\t\ttaskFile := filepath.Join(planDir, id+\".md\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf(\"const %s = await runs.run('%s', {agent:'worker', task:'按 %s 执行 %s，完成后 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent 写入 tasks.json'});\\n\",\n\t\t\tid, id, taskFile, id))\n\t}\n\tsb.WriteString(\"return {\")\n\tfor i, id := range ids {\n\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\", \")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(id + \": \" + id + \".output\")\n\t}\n\tsb.WriteString(\"};\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"`;\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"```\\n\\n\")\n\tsb.WriteString(\"把上述 `workflowScript` 作为 `subagent` 工具调用的 `workflowScript` 参数触发编排执行。\\n\")\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n\n// EnsureTasksJSON writes the initial doing/tasks.json draft when it does not\n// exist yet: task list + dependencies (from plan/task*.md) + status=pending.\n// It is idempotent (existing tasks.json is left untouched).\nfunc EnsureTasksJSON(doingDir, planDir string) error {\n\tif doingDir == \"\" || planDir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"doingDir and planDir cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\ttasksJSONPath := filepath.Join(doingDir, \"tasks.json\")\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(tasksJSONPath); err == nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\ttasks := scanPlanOrchTasks(planDir)\n\tif len(tasks) == 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"no task*.md files found in plan directory %s\", planDir)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(doingDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tb.WriteString(\"{\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0\\\",\\n  \\\"tasks\\\": [\\n\")\n\tfor i, t := range tasks {\n\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\tb.WriteString(\",\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tdeps := \"[]\"\n\t\tif len(t.Dependencies) > 0 {\n\t\t\tdeps = \"[\"\n\t\t\tfor j, d := range t.Dependencies {\n\t\t\t\tif j > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\tdeps += \", \"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tdeps += fmt.Sprintf(\"%q\", d)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tdeps += \"]\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf(\"    {\\\"task_id\\\": %q, \\\"task_name\\\": %q, \\\"task_file\\\": %q, \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\", \\\"dependencies\\\": %s, \\\"attempts\\\": 0}\",\n\t\t\tt.ID, t.ID, t.ID+\".md\", deps))\n\t}\n\tb.WriteString(\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\")\n\treturn os.WriteFile(tasksJSONPath, []byte(b.String()), 0644)\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1005,"output":5164,"cacheRead":182400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2707,"totalTokens":188569,"cost":{"input":0.00043717500000000004,"output":0.00449268,"cacheRead":0.0006612,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005591054999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912727095,"responseId":"17b48642-8a16-4f1c-ad19-57657fd4c59d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_8o4rHYaP8oKnbmTbl2NH6213","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 7744 bytes to /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/builder/orchestration.go"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912773233}]}
