end` (dead)\n- `loadDoingLoopContent` (used by easy_prompt.go)\n- `formatTaskInfoSection` (dead, uses parser)\n- `formatKeyResults` (dead, used by formatTaskInfoSection)\n- `formatDebugContext` (dead, uses parser)\n\nSo I'll rewrite `doing_prompt.go` to keep ONLY `loadDoingLoopContent`. And `stripYAMLFrontmatter` is in easy_prompt.go (same package). So loadDoingLoopContent can call stripYAMLFrontmatter.\n\nActually, wait — is `loadDoingLoopContent` used anywhere in the builder? No, the builder has its own `renderDoingLoop`. `loadDoingLoopContent` is only used by easy_prompt.go. And easy_prompt.go itself is dead (only tests use GenerateEasyPromptFile/GenerateEasyPrompt). Hmm.\n\nLet me check: is `easy_prompt.go` used in production? The handler/easy.go uses `builder.SaveEasyPrompt` (builder package), NOT `prompt.GenerateEasyPromptFile`. So `prompt/easy_prompt.go` is dead production code too!\n\nBut `easy_prompt_test.go` and `debug_skill_verify_test.go` test it. These tests don't import parser. So I could keep easy_prompt.go (it doesn't need to import parser after I inline ExtractBugFrontmatter).\n\nActually, let me minimize: keep `easy_prompt.go` (it's tested and doesn't need parser after inlining), rewrite `doing_prompt.go` to keep only `loadDoingLoopContent`, delete context.go + context_test.go + doing_prompt_test.go, rewrite integration_test.go + integration_rfc001_test.go + plan_prompt_test.go + context_helpers.go.\n\nActually, `easy_prompt.go`'s `loadDebugContextLocal` uses `parser.ExtractBugFrontmatter`. I'll replace with a local inline implementation (or use workspace.ExtractBugFrontmatter? But prompt importing workspace — does prompt import workspace? Let me check: doing_prompt.go imports workspace. easy_prompt.go imports parser only (for ExtractBugFrontmatter). If I import workspace in easy_prompt.go, is there a cycle? workspace imports nothing from prompt. prompt imports workspace in doing_prompt.go already. So prompt → workspace is fine. But actually, let me check if workspace imports prompt. No. So I can use `workspace.ExtractBugFrontmatter` in easy_prompt.go.\n\nWait, but there might be a subtle issue: does `internal/prompt` importing `internal/workspace` create a cycle with anything? Let me check: workspace imports only stdlib. prompt imports workspace (already in doing_prompt.go). No cycle. \n\nSo in easy_prompt.go, I'll replace `parser.ExtractBugFrontmatter` with `workspace.ExtractBugFrontmatter`. That's clean and avoids duplicating.\n\nActually, even simpler: inline a tiny extractor in easy_prompt.go to avoid the workspace import. But workspace import is already there via doing_prompt.go (which I'm shrinking). Let me check if doing_prompt.go after shrinking still imports workspace. `loadDoingLoopContent` doesn't need workspace. So if I shrink doing_prompt.go to just loadDoingLoopContent, it won't import workspace anymore. Then easy_prompt.go would need the workspace import for ExtractBugFrontmatter.\n\nHmm, but easy_prompt.go already imports `os`, `path/filepath`, `sort`, `strings`, `fmt`. Adding workspace import is fine. But wait — does easy_prompt.go already import workspace? No. Let me just inline the extractor in easy_prompt.go to keep it self-contained. It's a tiny function.\n\nLet me inline:\n```go\nfunc extractBugFrontmatter(content string) (summary, status string) {\n    ... (same logic)\n}\n```\n\nAnd replace `parser.ExtractBugFrontmatter` with `extractBugFrontmatter`.\n\nOK let me now do the prompt package changes.\n\nStep 1: Delete context.go and context_test.go and doing_prompt_test.go.\nStep 2: Rewrite doing_prompt.go to minimal (just loadDoingLoopContent).\nStep 3: Rewrite easy_prompt.go: remove parser import, inline extractBugFrontmatter, remove check_command/check_step_header SetVariable.\nStep 4: Rewrite context_helpers.go: remove formatOKRContent/formatSPECContent + parser import.\nStep 5: Rewrite plan_prompt_test.go (remove parser tests).\nStep 6: Rewrite integration_test.go (remove parser tests).\nStep 7: Rewrite integration_rfc001_test.go (remove parser tests).\n\nLet me start. First delete files."}}
