{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Prompt package passes. Now let me handle the handler package:\n1. Rewrite `handler/doing.go` — remove executor/git/parser imports, add orchestration + runtime.Run + gate + MaxRetries.\n2. Rewrite `handler/learning.go` — migrate to workspace readers.\n3. Delete/rewrite test files: doing_test.go, learning_test.go, git_test.go.\n\nAlso `handler/doing.go` has `loadTasksFromPlan` (uses parser) and `printExecutionSummary` (uses executor), `commitDoingResults` (uses git), `ensureGitInitialized`/`ensureGitUserConfigured` (uses git via exec). I need to remove the executor/parser/git imports and their usages.\n\nLet me design the new handler/doing.go.\n\nNew `Doing` flow:\n```go\nfunc Doing(jobID string, opts Options) error {\n    cfg := LoadConfig()\n    rickDir := workspace.GetRickDir()\n    jobDir := .../jobs/jobID\n    planDir := .../plan\n    doingDir := .../doing\n    validate jobDir, planDir\n    MkdirAll doingDir\n\n    // Ensure tasks.json initial draft\n    if err := builder.EnsureTasksJSON(doingDir, planDir); err != nil {\n        return ...\n    }\n\n    maxRetries := cfg.MaxRetries\n    if maxRetries <= 0 { maxRetries = 3 }\n\n    for attempt := 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++ {\n        // build prompt (orchestration of pending tasks)\n        promptFile, method, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(doingDir, planDir, rickDir, jobID)\n        if err != nil { return ... }\n\n        // run pi\n        _, _, err = runtime.NewPiRuntime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...).Run(method, promptFile, cfg)\n        if err != nil {\n            // workflow not triggered / session not settled → retry\n            if attempt < maxRetries { continue }\n            return fmt.Errorf(\"...: %w\", err)\n        }\n\n        // gate\n        if err := runGate(doingDir); err != nil {\n            if attempt < maxRetries { continue }\n            return fmt.Errorf(\"gate failed: %w\", err)\n        }\n        return nil\n    }\n    return ...\n}\n```\n\nWhere `runGate(doingDir)` invokes `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doingDir>`. I need to resolve the rickDir for the helper path. The helper is at `<rickDir>/skills/rick-gates/helper.py`. Since `rickDir` = `.rick` in cwd, I can compute `filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\", \"rick-gates\", \"helper.py\")`.\n\nLet me write `runGate`:\n```go\nfunc runGate(doingDir, rickDir string) error {\n    helper := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\", \"rick-gates\", \"helper.py\")\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"python3\", helper, doingDir)\n    out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"gate failed: %s\", strings.TrimSpace(string(out)))\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\nThe test asserts `doing.go` contains `MaxRetries`. So I need a literal `MaxRetries` in the code. I'll use `maxRetries := cfg.MaxRetries` — that contains \"MaxRetries\". Good. But wait, the test does `if 'MaxRetries' not in doing_src`. So `cfg.MaxRetries` contains \"MaxRetries\". Good.\n\nAlso the test checks doing.go doesn't import `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/executor\"`, `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/git\"`, `\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"`. So I must not import those.\n\nNow, what about the old helper functions in doing.go: `loadTasksFromPlan`, `sortTaskFiles`, `extractTaskNumber`, `printExecutionSummary`, `commitDoingResults`, `ensureGitUserConfigured`, `ensureGitInitialized`? These are used by:\n- `loadTasksFromPlan` — used by Doing and DoingDryRun. I'll remove it (or keep a version without parser? Actually DoingDryRun will now use builder orchestration directly). Remove.\n- `printExecutionSummary` — used by Doing. Remove.\n- `commitDoingResults` — used by Doing. Remove (commit now done by pi).\n- `ensureGitUserConfigured`, `ensureGitInitialized` — used by Doing. These don't import executor/parser/git packages — they use `os/exec` directly. But `ensureGitInit