{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_00_ET_oNAhxPdfAJ3NIEvJezkm1709","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && sed -i 's/act-path/runtime trace/g' .rick/skills/zero_retry_task_design_skill/skill.md && grep -rn \"act-path\\|act_path\" .rick/ || echo \"NONE\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":".rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks/task4/raw_session_coding.log:13586:{\"type\":\"turn_end\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I have a very good understanding. Let me proceed with the migration. I'll do it systematically:\\n\\n1. Create `internal/runtime/` with migrated files (cli.go, executor.go, agentdir.go, runtime.go) + migrated test files (cli_test.go, executor_test.go, agentdir_test.go, cli_mock_test.go, executor_e2e_test.go, executor_realpi_smoke_test.go, executor_realds_test.go).\\n\\n2. Update package names from `piagent` to `runtime`, and update import path references in tests (`github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/agent/piagent` → nothing needed since tests are same package; but executor_e2e_test.go imports actpath + agent, which stay same). The realpi smoke test comment `./internal/agent/piagent/...` → `./internal/runtime/...`.\\n\\n3. Delete old `internal/agent/piagent/` directory.\\n\\n4. Update all cmd source + test files: import path + qualifier.\\n\\n5. Add `isSessionReady` function + test.\\n\\n6. Add `Runtime` interface, `piRuntime`, `Trace` in runtime.go.\\n\\n7. config: add `Runtime` field, default, normalization + test.\\n\\nLet me think about the package name `runtime` and potential conflicts within the runtime package test files. The test files will be `package runtime`. The `executor_e2e_test.go` imports `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/actpath` and `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/agent`. No conflict with `runtime` package name.\\n\\nWait — one issue: within the `internal/runtime` package, the `executor.go` imports `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/agent`. And the package itself is `runtime`. That's fine.\\n\\nNow let me also think about the `cli_mock_test.go` — it imports `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config` and uses `config.Config`. Fine.\\n\\nNow, about the `runtime.go` file with the `Runtime` interface and `piRuntime` skeleton and `Trace` struct. Let me design it carefully.\\n\\n```go\\npackage runtime\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/agent\\\"\\n\\t\\\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config\\\"\\n)\\n\\n// Trace is the behavioral trace of a single runtime run. It carries the\\n// information the old act-path + session pair held: the session identity, the\\n// tool-call history, the agent's final message, the raw log path, the self-timed\\n// duration, and whether the runtime reported a clean settle.\\ntype Trace struct {\\n\\tSessionID    string\\n\\tToolCalls    []agent.ToolCall\\n\\tFinalMessage string\\n\\tRawLogPath   string\\n\\tDuration     time.Duration\\n\\tSettled      bool\\n}\\n\\n// Runtime is the seam for agent runtimes (pi today, dsh later). Handlers depend\\n// on this interface rather than a concrete piRuntime, so adding a new runtime\\n// (e.g. dsh) means implementing and registering dshRuntime without touching the\\n// handlers or the method-layer templates.\\ntype Runtime interface {\\n\\tName() string\\n\\tRun(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (sessionID string, trace *Trace, err error)\\n}\\n\\n// piRuntime implements Runtime for the pi coding agent.\\ntype piRuntime struct {\\n\\tpiPath    string\\n\\textraArgs []string\\n}\\n\\n// NewPiRuntime constructs the pi runtime implementation.\\nfunc NewPiRuntime(piPath string, extraArgs ...string) *piRuntime {\\n\\treturn &piRuntime{piPath: piPath, extraArgs: extraArgs}\\n}\\n\\nfunc (r *piRuntime) Name() string { return \\\"pi\\\" }\\n\\n// Run launches pi for one prompt. methodText is the method-layer system prompt:\\n// it is written to a temp file (cleaned up on return) and injected via\\n// `--append-system-prompt <methodFile>` so pi keeps its default skeleton while\\n// rick's method is prepended to the session. promptFile carries the user prompt\\n// (instance context). It returns the parsed session id + trace.\\n//\\n// This is the runtime contract's skeleton; the final Run signature lands with\\n// task8's Execute→Run switch. Execute below (the AgentExecutor-compatible path)\\n// remains the wired entry point for now.\\nfunc (r *piRuntime) Run(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (string, *Trace, error) {\\n\\t// Resolve the pi binary.\\n\\tpiBin := r.piPath\\n\\tif piBin == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tpiBin = piPathOrDefault(cfg)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// methodText goes through a temp file (avoid long inline argv); removed when done.\\n\\tvar methodFile string\\n\\tif methodText != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tf, err := os.CreateTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"rick-method-*.md\\\")\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"create method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tmethodFile = f.Name()\\n\\t\\tif _, err := f.WriteString(methodText); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tf.Close()\\n\\t\\t\\tos.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"write method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif err := f.Close(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tos.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"close method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tdefer os.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Raw session log: the runtime writes the raw JSONL somewhere for the trace.\\n\\t// (task8's cutover will route this to the job dir; the skeleton keeps it in\\n\\t// a temp file alongside the method file.)\\n\\trawLog, err := os.CreateTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"rick-raw-*.log\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"create raw log temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n\\trawLogPath := rawLog.Name()\\n\\trawLog.Close()\\n\\tdefer os.Remove(rawLogPath)\\n\\n\\t// Build args: --mode json [extraArgs] --append-system-prompt <methodFile> <promptFile>\\n\\tmerged := mergeExtraArgs(cfg, r.extraArgs)\\n\\targs := make([]string, 0, len(merged)+6)\\n\\targs = append(args, \\\"--mode\\\", \\\"json\\\")\\n\\targs = append(args, merged...)\\n\\tif methodFile != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\targs = append(args, \\\"--append-system-prompt\\\", methodFile)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif promptFile != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\targs = append(args, promptFile)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tcmd := exec.Command(piBin, args...)\\n\\tcmd.Env = AgentEnv()\\n\\tstdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tsess, parseErr := parseStream(stdout, rawLogPath)\\n\\tcmd.Wait() //nolint\\n\\tif parseErr != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, parseErr\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\ttrace := &Trace{\\n\\t\\tSessionID:    sess.sessionID,\\n\\t\\tToolCalls:    sess.toolCalls,\\n\\t\\tFinalMessage: sess.finalMessage,\\n\\t\\tRawLogPath:   sess.rawLogPath,\\n\\t\\tDuration:     sess.duration,\\n\\t\\tSettled:      sess.settled,\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn sess.sessionID, trace, nil\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHmm, but wait — the `Trace.RawLogPath` points to a temp file that gets removed via defer. That's a bit odd but acceptable for a skeleton. Actually, since the raw log is deleted right after, the Trace.RawLogPath would point to a non-existent file. For a skeleton that's fine, but let me reconsider.\\n\\nActually, the task says the temp file for methodText should be \\\"临时文件由 runtime 创建并 defer 清理、用完即删\\\". The raw log is different — it's the session trace. For the skeleton, maybe I should keep the raw log path but not delete it (or delete it). Let me keep it simple: the raw log is created via `parseStream` which needs a path. For the skeleton, I'll write it to a temp file and NOT delete it (or delete it). Since it's a skeleton and task8 will route it properly, I'll use a temp file for the raw log and leave it (not delete) — actually, to be clean, I'll delete the method file (as required) but keep the raw log.\\n\\nHmm, actually let me reconsider the whole `Run` design. The key result says:\\n\\n\\\"`Run` 启动 pi 时把 `methodText` 落盘临时文件、经 `--append-system-prompt <method文件路径>` 注入... 临时文件由 runtime 创建并 defer 清理、用完即删, `promptFile` 作为 user prompt\\\"\\n\\nThe most important testable bits:\\n1. `type Runtime interface` with `Name() string` and `Run(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (sessionID string, trace *Trace, err error)`.\\n2. `piRuntime` struct.\\n3. `type Trace struct`.\\n4. `--append-system-prompt` string in source.\\n5. `methodText string`, `promptFile string`, `cfg *config.Config`, `*Trace` in source.\\n\\nThe test script checks for these strings in `runtime_src_txt` (concatenation of non-test .go files in internal/runtime). So as long as my `runtime.go` contains those strings, the test passes. The actual behavior of Run is not directly tested by task4.py (it only greps for the strings + builds + runs tests).\\n\\nBut I want the code to be correct and compilable, and ideally I'd add a test for `Run`'s temp file + --append-system-prompt behavior. But I should be careful: the test script `task4.py` runs `go test ./internal/runtime/...` which runs ALL tests including any new ones I add. So I need my added tests to pass.\\n\\nLet me decide on the scope of `Run`. I'll implement it functionally so it actually works, and I can optionally add a test. But adding a test for Run requires a mock pi binary that records argv (proving --append-system-prompt <file> is passed and promptFile is the user prompt). That's valuable and matches the key result's spirit. But I need to be careful not to over-engineer.\\n\\nActually, let me keep it focused. The key deliverables and their tests:\\n\\n1. Package migration + compile green (build + test).\\n2. isSessionReady + test.\\n3. config runtime field + normalization + test.\\n4. Runtime interface + piRuntime + Trace + --append-system-prompt.\\n\\nFor #4, the test script only greps for strings. But I want at least a minimal test for Run to demonstrate it works. Let me add a test that:\\n- Creates a mock pi that writes its argv to a file (like writeMockPi).\\n- Calls `NewPiRuntime(mockPi).Run(\\\"method text\\\", \\\"prompt.md\\\", nil)`.\\n- Asserts argv contains `--append-system-prompt` followed by a temp file path (which contains \\\"method text\\\"), and `prompt.md` is last.\\n- Asserts the method temp file is removed after Run (the --append-system-prompt file path no longer exists).\\n- Asserts sessionID returned matches the mock's emitted session.\\n\\nBut wait, `Run` needs the mock pi to emit a valid JSONL stream so `parseStream` succeeds. The mock pi (writeMockPiEmitting) prints a stream. But writeMockPiEmitting uses `cat <<EOF` which doesn't capture argv. I need a mock that BOTH writes argv AND emits JSONL. Let me write a combined mock.\\n\\nActually, let me keep the Run test simpler: the mock pi writes argv to a file AND emits a minimal JSONL stream (session + agent_settled). Then verify:\\n- argv has `--mode json`, `--append-system-prompt <file>`, `<promptFile>`.\\n- The method file content == \\\"method text\\\".\\n- The method file is removed after Run returns.\\n- sessionID == \\\"s123\\\".\\n\\nThis is a solid test. Let me write it.\\n\\nActually, wait — I need to think about whether the `Run`'s raw log temp file cleanup. Let me simplify: for the skeleton, I'll have `Run` write the raw log to a temp file and NOT delete it (the trace needs a valid path). Actually, simpler: I'll reuse the raw log temp file and delete it via defer too, since it's a skeleton. But then `Trace.RawLogPath` points to deleted file. Hmm.\\n\\nLet me reconsider. Actually, for cleanliness and to avoid a dangling pointer, let me have `Run` NOT delete the raw log (leave it as the trace artifact). It's created in a temp dir. Actually `os.CreateTemp` with empty dir uses the system temp dir. That's a bit messy.\\n\\nLet me reconsider the whole thing. Maybe simpler: `Run` should be a skeleton that demonstrates the contract but doesn't need to fully run pi. But key result 6 explicitly describes Run's behavior (temp file + --append-system-prompt + promptFile). \\n\\nI think the cleanest is:\\n- `Run` writes methodText to temp file (defer remove).\\n- `Run` creates raw log in temp (for parseStream), and I'll keep it simple by NOT removing it — but that leaks. Alternatively, parseStream writes to the raw log; I can point rawLogPath to a temp file and remove it after, but then trace.RawLogPath is stale.\\n\\nGiven this is a skeleton and task8 will finalize, I'll make a pragmatic choice:\\n- Use `os.CreateTemp` for the raw log, get its path, close it.\\n- defer os.Remove(rawLogPath) — clean up.\\n- trace.RawLogPath = rawLogPath (may be stale after cleanup, but skeleton).\\n\\nActually, you know what, let me reconsider. The point of the raw log in the current Executor is to persist the session for act-path. In `Run`, the trace carries ToolCalls etc. directly, so the raw log isn't strictly needed as a persistent artifact for the skeleton. I'll just use a temp raw log and clean it up. This is fine.\\n\\nActually, even simpler: I can avoid the raw log file entirely by having `parseStream` accept an empty path? No, it always opens the file. Let me not change parseStream's signature (to keep the existing tests passing). I'll create a temp raw log file and clean it up.\\n\\nOK let me also double-check: does `Run` need to handle the case where methodText is empty? Yes — if empty, skip the --append-system-prompt flag. The key result says methodText is injected via --append-system-prompt; if empty, we skip. Good.\\n\\nNow, there's another consideration: the `Run` signature returns `(sessionID string, trace *Trace, err error)`. The test script checks for `*Trace` string (in the return). My signature `(string, *Trace, error)` contains `*Trace`. Good. And `methodText string`, `promptFile string`, `cfg *config.Config` must appear. My signature `Run(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config)` contains all three. Good. And `Name() string` for the interface method. Good.\\n\\nNow let me also make sure the interface method signature matches the test script's expected strings. The interface:\\n```go\\ntype Runtime interface {\\n\\tName() string\\n\\tRun(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (sessionID string, trace *Trace, err error)\\n}\\n```\\nThis contains `Name() string`, `methodText string`, `promptFile string`, `cfg *config.Config`, `*Trace`, `type Runtime interface`. \\n\\nAnd `piRuntime` struct + `NewPiRuntime`. And `type Trace struct`. Good.\\n\\nNow, let me write everything.\\n\\nFirst, let me create the migrated files. I'll use `git mv`? Actually, the old directory is tracked in git. But the task says delete the old package. Since the old files are tracked, I should `git mv` to preserve history, but since I'm also changing content (package name), it's easier to just create new files and delete old. Actually, using `git mv` then edit is cleaner for git history but more steps. Let me just do it with cp + edits + rm, then git add will detect renames.\\n\\nLet me start by creating the new directory and copying files.\\n\\nActually, the cleanest and least error-prone: use `mkdir` + `cp` the 3 source + 7 test files, then edit package name in each, then add runtime.go, then delete old dir.\\n\\nLet me list all files to migrate:\\nSource:\\n- cli.go\\n- executor.go\\n- agentdir.go\\nTests:\\n- cli_test.go\\n- executor_test.go\\n- agentdir_test.go\\n- cli_mock_test.go\\n- executor_e2e_test.go\\n- executor_realpi_smoke_test.go\\n- executor_realds_test.go\\n\\nLet me do the copy and then edit.\\n\\nActually, for efficiency, let me use bash to copy all files, then use edit tool for package renames, then handle the rest.\\n\\nLet me proceed step by step.\\n\\nStep 1: Create internal/runtime dir and copy files.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"reasoning_content\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I now have a full understanding of the task. Let me read the referenced skills and then start executing the migration.\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_00_aW9NhM0rYSl3Ky0a4o2W8681\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/skills/verify_go_changes_skill/skill.md\"}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_01_Zbveh9p8E3yZmOqGLMMf6720\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/skills/global_ref_sync_skill/skill.md\"}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_02_nYcEsC6mV03QPqZay6548871\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/skills/pi_runtime_verification_skill/skill.md\"}}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"deepseek\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-pro\",\"usage\":{\"input\":7492,\"output\":3969,\"cacheRead\":74368,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"reasoning\":3756,\"totalTokens\":85829,\"cost\":{\"input\":0.00325902,\"output\":0.00345303,\"cacheRead\":0.000269584,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0.0069816340000000005}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1786902112830,\"responseId\":\"fe7dae1b-d8c9-4f4a-a06a-a11a4f17fca8\",\"rawStopReason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"toolResults\":[{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_00_aW9NhM0rYSl3Ky0a4o2W8681\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# skill:verify-go-changes（验证 Go 代码修改）\\n\\n## 触发场景\\n\\n修改了 Go 源文件后，需要验证编译通过、单元测试和集成测试通过时使用。\\n\\n## 预期效果\\n\\n- 编译无报错\\n- 单元测试全绿（精确匹配改动包，不跑全量）\\n- 集成测试通过\\n- dry-run 输出包含正确注入内容\\n\\n## 核心内容\\n\\n### Step 1：编译检查\\n\\n```bash\\ngo build ./...\\n# 或使用辅助脚本：\\npython3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/build_rick.py\\n```\\n\\n### Step 2：单元测试（精确范围，禁止 ./internal/...）\\n\\n```bash\\n# 只跑改动的包，避免混入依赖真实 API key 的无关测试\\ngo test ./internal/prompt/... -v\\ngo test ./internal/executor/... -v\\ngo test ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s -v\\n```\\n\\n**禁止**：`go test ./internal/...` 全量，会混入依赖真实环境的无关测试。\\n\\n### Step 3：集成测试（如有）\\n\\n```bash\\nbash tests/tools_integration_test.sh\\n```\\n\\n### Step 4：dry-run 验证注入效果\\n\\n```bash\\n./bin/rick doing job_N --dry-run | grep \\\"关键词\\\"\\n./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep -c '{{未替换变量}}'  # 应为 0\\n```\\n\\n### Go test 超时问题\\n\\n如果测试卡住 > 30s（卡在 retry sleep），检查是否有全局 `~/.rick/config.json` 设置了高 `max_retries`：\\n\\n```go\\n// 在测试函数开头添加：\\ndir := t.TempDir()\\nt.Setenv(\\\"HOME\\\", dir)\\n_ = os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(dir, \\\".rick\\\"), 0755)\\n_ = os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, \\\".rick\\\", \\\"config.json\\\"), []byte(`{\\\"max_retries\\\":2}`), 0644)\\n```\\n\\n### DIP 验证命令\\n\\n修改 internal/ 模块后验证依赖倒置是否保持：\\n\\n```bash\\n# 确认 executor/actpath 不直接依赖 claudecode\\ngrep -r \\\"claudecode\\\" internal/executor/ internal/actpath/ 2>/dev/null\\n# 应无输出（仅 doing.go 可引用 claudecode）\\n```\\n\\n### embed.FS 变更后必须重新构建\\n\\n模板文件（`internal/prompt/templates/`）通过 embed.FS 编译进二进制，改后必须：\\n\\n```bash\\n./scripts/build.sh  # 重新构建才能生效\\n./bin/rick doing job_N --dry-run  # 验证新内容\\n```\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1786902166499},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_01_Zbveh9p8E3yZmOqGLMMf6720\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# skill:global-ref-sync（修改核心名称前全局同步）\\n\\n## 触发场景\\n\\n修改一个在多个文件中被引用的核心名称/变量时：\\n- 重命名 skill 名称（如 `sense_skill_path` → `grilling_skill_path`）\\n- 更换模板变量名（如 `{{job_okr_content}}` → `{{loops_context}}`）\\n- 重命名 Go 函数/接口（如删除 `loadOKRPath`）\\n\\n信号词：「将 X 替换为 Y」「重命名 X」「移除 X 的所有引用」\\n\\n## 预期效果\\n\\n- 一次规划所有需改动文件，不遗漏\\n- 避免\\\"改了 A，跑测试才发现 B/C/D 也要改\\\"的反复循环\\n\\n## 核心内容\\n\\n### 第 0 步（禁止跳过）：全局 grep 找出所有引用\\n\\n```bash\\n# 在整个项目中查找旧名称\\ngrep -rn \\\"旧名称\\\" internal/ .rick/ --include=\\\"*.go\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\"\\n```\\n\\n列出所有包含旧名称的文件，然后逐一规划修改。\\n\\n### 第 1 步：规划改动文件清单\\n\\n将 grep 结果按文件分组，确认每个文件的修改类型：Replace / Delete / Add\\n\\n### 第 1.5 步（Edit 前）：精确定位目标行\\n\\nEdit 工具要求 old_string 与文件内容完全匹配。直接构造 old_string 容易因行序/缩进不符导致失败。\\n\\n**正确流程**：\\n1. `Read` 目标文件的精确行范围（用 offset/limit 缩窄）\\n2. 从 Read 输出中复制目标行，粘贴为 old_string\\n3. 再调用 Edit\\n\\n**反模式**：凭记忆拼 old_string → Edit 报错 → 再 Read → 重试（浪费一轮）\\n\\n### 第 2 步：按依赖顺序修改\\n\\n推荐顺序（避免编译中断）：\\n1. 核心定义文件（Go 源码中的常量/函数名）\\n2. 模板文件（doing.md、plan.md 等 `.md` 模板）\\n3. 测试文件（`*_test.go`、`test*.py`）\\n4. 文档文件（`.rick/` 下的 .md 文件）\\n\\n### 第 3 步：二次确认无遗漏\\n\\n```bash\\n# 验证旧名称已彻底清除\\ngrep -rn \\\"旧名称\\\" internal/ .rick/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\".git\\\"\\n# 应返回 0 行\\n```\\n\\n### 第 4 步：build + 测试\\n\\n```bash\\ngo build ./... && go test ./internal/...\\n```\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1786902166499},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_02_nYcEsC6mV03QPqZay6548871\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"---\\nname: pi-runtime-verification\\ndescription: 迁移/更换 rick 的 agent runtime（如 claude→pi）后，做真实命令级端到端验证\\n---\\n\\n# Skill: pi runtime 迁移的命令级端到端验证\\n\\n## 触发场景\\n\\n当 rick 迁移或更换底层 agent runtime（如 claude code → pi，或 pi 版本大升级），且改动涉及 rick 调用 agent 的 CLI flags / 事件解析 / prompt 落盘路径时使用。\\n\\n**问题信号**：\\n- 只在 piagent 包内部写了单测（mock binary），没跑过真实 `rick <cmd>`\\n- 研究 brief 说某 flag \\\"接受 id\\\" 但没说\\\"加载 vs 创建\\\"语义\\n- 改动跨多个 cmd 文件（plan/easy/doing/learning/human-loop/ctrl/dream）\\n\\n## 预期效果\\n\\n- 暴露\\\"包内部测试通过但真实命令失败\\\"的隐藏 bug（如 `--session` 加载 vs 创建语义）\\n- 确保 prompt 落盘到 rick 标准 job 目录（非 /tmp），完全对齐 rick 功能\\n- 防止\\\"研究 brief 描述正确但语义未验证\\\"导致的迁移 bug 流入提交\\n\\n## 核心内容\\n\\n### 1. 每个命令逐个真实跑（非 dry-run）\\n\\ninteractive 命令（plan/easy/learning/human-loop/ctrl）用管道喂 stdin 模拟一轮对话：\\n```bash\\necho \\\"请直接回复: <CMD>_OK\\\" | timeout 200 ./bin/rick <cmd> [args] 2>&1 | tail -8\\n```\\nprint/json 命令（doing 走 Execute()、dream --background）能自动完成。\\n\\n### 2. 三项必须验证\\n\\n| 项 | 验证方法 |\\n|---|---|\\n| prompt 落盘 | `find .rick/jobs -name \\\"*_prompt.md\\\" -newer <ref>` 确认在 job_N/doing/prompts/ 下（非 /tmp） |\\n| pi 真实响应 | 输出含 `<CMD>_OK`（证明 pi 读了 prompt + 真实 LLM 回复） |\\n| exit code | 0（interactive 命令 pi 处理完应正常退出） |\\n\\n### 3. flag 语义验证（关键，防 brief 误判）\\n\\n研究 brief 若说\\\"X flag 接受 id\\\"，**不要直接信**——要单独测其\\\"加载已有 vs 创建新\\\"语义：\\n```bash\\n# 测创建语义: 用一个不存在的 id\\necho OK | pi --provider <p> --model <m> --<flag> newuuid123 /dev/null 2>&1 | head -3\\n# 看输出是 \\\"No session found\\\"（加载语义，错）还是 \\\"creating a new session\\\"（创建语义，对）\\n```\\n\\n### 4. 用 doing 做全链路（Execute + 解析器 + actpath）\\n\\ndoing 走 `piagent.Execute()`（json 解析），能验证解析器在真实 LLM 工具调用下正确：\\n```bash\\n# 给 job 造最小 plan（task1.md 无依赖 + 简单测试方法）\\necho \\\"请直接回复: DOING_OK\\\" | ./bin/rick doing <job> 2>&1 | tail\\n# 确认: pi 真实建文件 + commit + task success\\ngit log --oneline -2  # 应见 pi 的 commit\\n```\\n\\n### 5. 验证失败时的处理\\n\\n发现的 bug 多是\\\"flag 语义误判\\\"或\\\"路径错\\\"——修复后必须**重跑该命令验证**，不能只改代码不验。\\n\\n### 6. 配置目录隔离验证（PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR，job_33 沉淀）\\n\\n改动涉及 `piagent.AgentEnv()`（所有 pi 子进程注入 `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=~/.rick/pi/agent`）时，四项必须验证：\\n\\n| 项 | 验证方法 | 通过标准 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| env 注入 | fake pi 脚本 `echo \\\"$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR\\\"` 断言 | 值 = 托管 agent dir |\\n| 隔离生效 | `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=/tmp/x pi list` + `pi install npm:y` | settings.json 写在 /tmp/x 下，且**保留未知字段**（hideThinkingBlock 等不被重写） |\\n| 包过滤 | settings.json 用对象形式 `{\\\"source\\\": ..., \\\"extensions\\\": []}` | `pi list` 显示 `(filtered)` 且**不会重写** settings.json |\\n| 真实加载 | `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=$HOME/.rick/pi/agent pi --mode json <provider/model/key flags> -p '列出可用工具'` | 输出含 subagent/web_search（扩展真的加载） |\\n\\n**已知边界（pi 内部行为）**：\\n- `pi install` 对 user scope 包在 managed 路径缺失时**回退全局 npm root**（`npm root -g`）复用代码——注册隔离、代码共享\\n- 隔离后 settings.json 无 provider/model → 直跑 pi 报 \\\"No API key found\\\"，必须带 CLI flags（rick 本就如此）\\n- `--session-id` 对不存在 id 打 Warning \\\"No project session found...creating a new session\\\" 是**正常创建语义**，不是错误\\n\\n### 7. 运行时自闭环验证（~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime，job_34 沉淀）\\n\\nrick 自闭环运行时 = 用 `npm install --prefix` 装**独立的 pi 包副本**，与全局 pi 完全隔离：\\n\\n| 事实 | 值 |\\n|------|-----|\\n| 安装 | `npm install --prefix ~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@<全局版本>`（全局有则匹配版本，pinned 失败降级 latest） |\\n| 二进制 | `~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi`（npm bin 软链 → 包内 dist/cli.js） |\\n| 解析优先级 | `cfg.PiPath` → 托管运行时（`piagent.RuntimeBin()`）→ PATH 的 `pi`（FindBinary / piPathOrDefault / piCommand / Executor 默认全部一致） |\\n| 版本锁定 | 与全局同版本（0.84.1）→ 行为连续；独立升级互不影响 |\\n| 测试隔离 | 测试用 `t.Setenv(\\\"HOME\\\", t.TempDir())` 或 `t.Setenv(\\\"RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR\\\", t.TempDir())` 让 RuntimeBin 解析到不存在路径 → 回退 PATH fake |\\n\\n验证命令：\\n```bash\\n~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi --version   # 托管版本\\nrick tools theme rick                                     # 主题写入 agent/themes/（配置隔离，job_33）\\npython3 -c \\\"import filecmp,os; print(filecmp.cmp('$HOME/.local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/modes/interactive/components/diff.js','$HOME/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/modes/interactive/components/diff.js',shallow=False))\\\"  # 运行时副本 = 原样（无 patch）\\n```\\n\\n**注意**：运行时副本保持 stock，不做代码级修改（用户决策，见 theme skill 第 7 节）。若未来要做运行时 patch（diff 反显→加粗、语法高亮等），需整函数替换保证幂等（锚点被消费），import 相对路径按文件层级算（diff.js 在 `dist/modes/interactive/components/` → utils 需 `../../../`）。\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1786902166499}]}\n.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks/task4/raw_session_coding.log:17070:{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_end\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"toolCall\":{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_00_KMeGXUNGmgzyU4kejv0P7133\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/runtime/runtime.go\",\"content\":\"package runtime\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os/exec\\\"\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/agent\\\"\\n\\t\\\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config\\\"\\n)\\n\\n// Trace is the behavioral trace of a single runtime run. It carries the same\\n// information the old act-path + session pair held: the session identity, the\\n// tool-call history, the agent's final message, the raw JSONL log path, the\\n// self-timed duration, and whether the runtime reported a clean settle.\\ntype Trace struct {\\n\\tSessionID    string\\n\\tToolCalls    []agent.ToolCall\\n\\tFinalMessage string\\n\\tRawLogPath   string\\n\\tDuration     time.Duration\\n\\tSettled      bool\\n}\\n\\n// Runtime is the seam for agent runtimes (pi today, dsh later). Handlers depend\\n// on this interface rather than a concrete piRuntime, so adding a new runtime\\n// means implementing and registering dshRuntime without touching the handlers\\n// or the method-layer templates.\\n//\\n// methodText is the method-layer system prompt (rick 方法描述): it is injected\\n// before the session via `--append-system-prompt <methodFile>` so pi keeps its\\n// default skeleton. promptFile is the instance context (user prompt).\\ntype Runtime interface {\\n\\tName() string\\n\\tRun(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (sessionID string, trace *Trace, err error)\\n}\\n\\n// piRuntime implements Runtime for the pi coding agent.\\ntype piRuntime struct {\\n\\tpiPath    string\\n\\textraArgs []string\\n}\\n\\n// NewPiRuntime constructs the pi runtime implementation. piPath may be empty\\n// (resolve via config / managed runtime / PATH); extraArgs are passed through to\\n// pi (e.g. --provider/--model/--api-key).\\nfunc NewPiRuntime(piPath string, extraArgs ...string) *piRuntime {\\n\\treturn &piRuntime{piPath: piPath, extraArgs: extraArgs}\\n}\\n\\n// Name returns the runtime's identifier (\\\"pi\\\").\\nfunc (r *piRuntime) Name() string { return \\\"pi\\\" }\\n\\n// Run launches pi for one prompt and returns the parsed session id + trace.\\n//\\n// methodText (the method layer) is written to a temp file and injected through\\n// `--append-system-prompt <methodFile>` — a session-preparation injection that\\n// preserves pi's default skeleton and avoids passing long text inline. The temp\\n// file is created by the runtime and removed on return (defer cleanup, deleted\\n// once used). promptFile is passed last as the user prompt (instance context).\\n//\\n// This is the runtime contract's skeleton: it is not yet wired into handlers\\n// (task8 performs the Execute→Run switch). The AgentExecutor-compatible Execute\\n// below remains the wired entry point for the structured doing path.\\nfunc (r *piRuntime) Run(methodText string, promptFile string, cfg *config.Config) (string, *Trace, error) {\\n\\tpiBin := r.piPath\\n\\tif piBin == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tpiBin = piPathOrDefault(cfg)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Method layer → temp file → --append-system-prompt <methodFile>. The runtime\\n\\t// owns the temp file and deletes it once pi has consumed it (defer).\\n\\tvar methodFile string\\n\\tif methodText != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tf, err := os.CreateTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"rick-method-*.md\\\")\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"create method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tmethodFile = f.Name()\\n\\t\\tif _, err := f.WriteString(methodText); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tf.Close()\\n\\t\\t\\tos.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"write method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif err := f.Close(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tos.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"close method temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tdefer os.Remove(methodFile)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Raw JSONL log: parseStream persists the event stream for the trace. The\\n\\t// skeleton keeps it in a temp file (task8 routes it to the job dir).\\n\\trawLog, err := os.CreateTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"rick-raw-*.log\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"create raw log temp file: %w\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n\\trawLogPath := rawLog.Name()\\n\\trawLog.Close()\\n\\tdefer os.Remove(rawLogPath)\\n\\n\\tmerged := mergeExtraArgs(cfg, r.extraArgs)\\n\\targs := make([]string, 0, len(merged)+6)\\n\\targs = append(args, \\\"--mode\\\", \\\"json\\\")\\n\\targs = append(args, merged...)\\n\\tif methodFile != \\\"\\\