g_check). But if I rebuild bin/rick, doing_check would be gone.\n\nThe task's Step 2 says to run `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. This is the check command for THIS task (task8). Since task8 deletes doing_check, there's a chicken-and-egg: after task8, doing_check is gone.\n\nLet me look at how the mark_task_success flow actually works. There's a `mark_task_success.py` script and the skill. The doing phase typically:\n1. Sub agent commits code.\n2. Runs `rick tools doing_check job_35` to verify.\n3. On pass, marks task success in tasks.json.\n\nBut task8 deletes doing_check. So the check for task8 must be different.\n\nActually, looking at the mark_task_success_skill/skill.md I just updated: it references rick-gates helper.py now. And there's `mark_task_success.py` and `build_rick.py` in that skill dir.\n\nLet me check what the actual flow is for marking task8 success. The key question: what does \"check pass\" mean for task8 now?\n\nThe outer prompt says to run `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. But that command is being deleted by task8 itself.\n\nHmm, actually, I think the answer is: the outer prompt (task8_doing_prompt.md) was generated BEFORE task8's changes, and it references the OLD doing_check. After task8 deletes doing_check, the correct \"check\" is the new gate (rick-gates helper.py) or the mark_task_success script.\n\nLet me look at the mark_task_success.py script to understand how it marks success and whether it calls doing_check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_1NITh8HFix7Te7qALHXc5269","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_vqJOfdfMCjqUhKJ3yoPn7470","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/build_rick.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":55,"output":3527,"cacheRead":253952,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3393,"totalTokens":257534,"cost":{"input":0.000023925000000000002,"output":0.00306849,"cacheRead":0.0009205760000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0040129910000000005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913266851,"responseId":"f812d188-d860-4d32-abf1-05f56e77e96d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_1NITh8HFix7Te7qALHXc5269","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Description: Mark a task as success in tasks.json with the current HEAD commit hash, then commit and verify doing_check passes.\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\n\n\ndef get_commit_hash():\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if r.returncode != 0:\n        return None, r.stderr.strip()\n    return r.stdout.strip(), None\n\n\ndef find_rick_root():\n    path = os.getcwd()\n    while path != \"/\":\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(path, \".rick\")):\n            return path\n        path = os.path.dirname(path)\n    return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Mark a task as success in tasks.json\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--job\", required=True, help=\"Job ID, e.g. job_17\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--task\", required=True, help=\"Task ID, e.g. task1\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--commit\", help=\"Commit hash (defaults to git HEAD)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--test\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Self-test mode\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if args.test:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": True, \"errors\": [], \"note\": \"self-test ok\"}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        return\n\n    root = find_rick_root()\n    if not root:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [\"cannot find .rick root\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    tasks_json = os.path.join(root, \".rick\", \"jobs\", args.job, \"doing\", \"tasks.json\")\n    if not os.path.exists(tasks_json):\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"tasks.json not found: {tasks_json}\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    commit_hash = args.commit\n    if not commit_hash:\n        commit_hash, err = get_commit_hash()\n        if err:\n            print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"git rev-parse failed: {err}\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n    with open(tasks_json, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        data = json.load(f)\n\n    now = datetime.now(tz=timezone(timedelta(hours=8))).isoformat()\n    found = False\n    for task in data[\"tasks\"]:\n        if task[\"task_id\"] == args.task:\n            task[\"status\"] = \"success\"\n            task[\"commit_hash\"] = commit_hash\n            task[\"updated_at\"] = now\n            found = True\n            break\n\n    if not found:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"task {args.task} not found in tasks.json\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    data[\"updated_at\"] = now\n    with open(tasks_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n    print(json.dumps({\"pass\": True, \"errors\": [], \"task\": args.task, \"commit_hash\": commit_hash}, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913309352},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_vqJOfdfMCjqUhKJ3yoPn7470","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Description: 构建 rick 并返回本地二进制路径，测试脚本用此代替系统安装版\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\n\ndef build_and_get_rick_bin(project_root=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Run `go build -o ./bin/rick ./cmd/rick` and return the path to the binary.\n    Always builds first to ensure the binary contains the latest code changes.\n\n    Returns (bin_path, error_message).\n    error_message is None on success.\n    \"\"\"\n    if project_root is None:\n        # Walk up to find project root (.rick/ dir)\n        current = os.path.abspath(os.getcwd())\n        while True:\n            if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(current, \".rick\")):\n                project_root = current\n                break\n            parent = os.path.dirname(current)\n            if parent == current:\n                return None, \"could not find project root (.rick/ directory)\"\n            current = parent\n\n    bin_path = os.path.join(project_root, \"bin\", \"rick\")\n    os.makedirs(os.path.join(project_root, \"bin\"), exist_ok=True)\n\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        [\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", bin_path, \"./cmd/rick\"],\n        cwd=project_root,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n    )\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        return None, f\"go build failed:\\n{result.stderr}\"\n\n    return bin_path, None\n\n\ndef main():\n    import argparse\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Build rick and return the path to the local binary\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--project-root\", default=None)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    bin_path, err = build_and_get_rick_bin(args.project_root)\n    if err:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"bin_path\": None, \"errors\": [err]}))\n        sys.exit(1)\n    print(json.dumps({\"pass\": True, \"bin_path\": bin_path, \"errors\": []}))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913309353},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the mark_task_success.py just marks the task success and commits. The \"doing_check\" verification is a separate concern. The actual flow for me (as the sub-agent doing task8) is:\n\n1. Commit my code changes.\n2. Run the check (which for task8 is now the new gate mechanism).\n3. Mark task8 success in tasks.json.\n\nBut the outer prompt's Step 2 says to run `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`.